<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Möngke</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Khan Möngke, Möngke Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mongke was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> from 1251 to 1259, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>. He sent his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>, leading to the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, and his brother Kublai against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>. He died during a campaign against the Song Dynasty in 1259, triggering a succession struggle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongke.jpg" alt="Möngke" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1438 artist, Shiraz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%B6ngke_enthroned._Tarikh-i_Jahangushay-i_Juvaini,_1438,_Shiraz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
